WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.140
Tap the tendon below your kneecap, and your leg kicks.

2
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.880
The path through the spinal cord has only one synapse between the sensor and the

3
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.100
motor neuron. Why only one?

4
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.280
And what does that same stretch do to the muscle on the other side of the joint?

5
00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:20.003
The sensor is a muscle spindle.

6
00:00:20.543 --> 00:00:23.783
It lies parallel to the ordinary fibres that make force.

7
00:00:24.763 --> 00:00:28.423
A tendon tap gives a brief stretch, and that stretches the spindle.

8
00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:32.703
Its 1A afferents respond to the speed and the amount of stretch.

9
00:00:33.343 --> 00:00:37.403
They fire. They enter the cord through the dorsal root, and they branch.

10
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:41.817
One branch excites the motor neurons of the same muscle, directly.

11
00:00:42.497 --> 00:00:46.417
That is one synapse, so the path is monosynaptic.

12
00:00:47.157 --> 00:00:48.897
These are alpha motor neurons.

13
00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:53.997
Their cell bodies sit in the ventral horn, and their axons leave through the ventral

14
00:00:53.997 --> 00:00:56.657
root. The muscle contracts against the stretch.

15
00:00:57.397 --> 00:00:59.017
Synergists get this branch too.

16
00:00:59.477 --> 00:01:02.257
The reflex as a whole is not purely monosynaptic.

17
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:07.607
The other branch excites an inhibitory interneuron, on the same side of the cord.

18
00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:12.727
That interneuron inhibits the motor neurons of the antagonist, the muscle that moves

19
00:01:12.727 --> 00:01:13.947
the joint the other way.

20
00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:17.567
This path has two synapses, so it is disynaptic.

21
00:01:18.187 --> 00:01:19.567
It stays on the same side.

22
00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:25.450
In decerebrate cats, Sherrington found that when a reflex excites one muscle, the

23
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.490
muscle that opposes it at the same joint relaxes.

24
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.250
He called the pairing reciprocal innervation.

25
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.330
The crossed extensor reflex is the one that crosses.

26
00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.830
A painful stimulus to one foot makes that leg withdraw, and the other leg takes the

27
00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.510
weight. It is polysynaptic and bilateral.

28
00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.550
The stretch reflex is local and one -sided.

29
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:48.683
So one stretch sends two commands.

30
00:01:49.403 --> 00:01:52.203
One synapse excites the motor neurons of the same muscle.

31
00:01:52.623 --> 00:01:57.243
Two synapses, through an interneuron on the same side, inhibit the antagonist.

32
00:01:57.903 --> 00:02:03.123
The rule to keep: a stretch excites the same muscle and inhibits its antagonist, on

33
00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:03.923
the same side.
